# report/: track the LaTeX sources, the Markdown logs and the built PDFs; ignore
# only LaTeX's intermediate files. (Was `report/` wholesale until 18 Sep 2026,
# which left the audit comment and the reports unreachable from a checkout.)
report/*.aux
report/*.log
report/*.out
report/*.toc
report/*.fls
report/*.fdb_latexmk
report/*.synctex.gz
HLS_CMDS/
papers/
# firmware/: PlatformIO build tree, and the golden vectors the native test reads
# (regenerate with `make firmware-coeffs`). The generated headers under
# lib/hls_filter/ ARE committed, including hls_clips.h -- the machine that builds
# the bench firmware then needs neither the dataset nor a Python environment.
firmware/.pio/
firmware/golden/
# Raw serial dumps from tools/capture_raw.py -- a run artifact, ~1.4 MB per
# 3-clip capture, scored into results/ and then of no further use.
capture*.bin
CLAUDE.md
